,{"type":122,"bibl":123},"discussion",[16],{"editor":125,"principal":128,"contributors":131,"change":146},{"_":126,"ref":127},"Jonathan Prag","#JP",{"_":129,"ref":130},"Valentina Mignosa","#VM",[132,135,138,142],{"_":126,"xml:id":133,"ref":134},"JP","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537",{"_":129,"xml:id":136,"ref":137},"VM","https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511",{"_":139,"xml:id":140,"ref":141},"Simona Stoyanova","SS","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9569",{"_":143,"xml:id":144,"ref":145},"Alessia Coccato","Coccato","https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6641-2820",{"_":147,"when":148,"who":130},"Valentina Mignosa created record and added metadata","2026-07-30",[],[151],"Manenti and Mignosa, 2024",[153],"XJUBNCHS",[155,155,156,18,23,27,157,157,158,159,160,161,162,110],"isic004521",{"_":4},"sabucina","sicilia","sicily","siracusa","museo archeologico regionale paolo orsi","ancient greek",[],{"title":165,"body":166,"divs":167,"editions":192,"images":202,"handnote":203},"ISic004521. ISic004521","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>ἔβαν? \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>ΕΒΑΝ?\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>  \u003Cspan>  \u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2> translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">  \u003C/p>\u003Cp>  \u003C/p>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The apparently complete text, written from left to right, is tentatively read as ἔβαν. The object bears a pencilled annotation reading “falso”, reflecting an earlier doubt about its authenticity. Although the forms of alpha and epsilon are compatible with the alphabet attested at Sabucina, the complete sequence does not correspond coherently to any identifiable Greek, indigenous or non-Sicilian alphabet, while the beta is anomalous in the area alphabetic tradition. The inscription should therefore be regarded as being of uncertain authenticity. The material itself does not resolve the question: comparable blackish limestone was used for the two inscribed statue bases dedicated respectively to Hieron II and to his son Gelon (ISic000823 and ISic003331).\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Manenti and Mignosa 2024 115-116 no.2 figs.4-6 \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\"> \u003Cp> Line 1  4-10  Interlineation line 1 to 2  not measured  \u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence \u003C/div>",[168,171,174,177,180,183,186,189],{"id":169,"html":170},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>ἔβαν? \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>ΕΒΑΝ?\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>",{"id":172,"html":173},"facsimile-images","\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>",{"id":175,"html":176},"apparatus","\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>  \u003Cspan>  \u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>",{"id":178,"html":179},"translation","\u003Ch2> translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">  \u003C/p>\u003Cp>  \u003C/p>",{"id":181,"html":182},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The apparently complete text, written from left to right, is tentatively read as ἔβαν. The object bears a pencilled annotation reading “falso”, reflecting an earlier doubt about its authenticity. Although the forms of alpha and epsilon are compatible with the alphabet attested at Sabucina, the complete sequence does not correspond coherently to any identifiable Greek, indigenous or non-Sicilian alphabet, while the beta is anomalous in the area alphabetic tradition. The inscription should therefore be regarded as being of uncertain authenticity. The material itself does not resolve the question: comparable blackish limestone was used for the two inscribed statue bases dedicated respectively to Hieron II and to his son Gelon (ISic000823 and ISic003331).\u003C/p>  ",{"id":184,"html":185},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Manenti and Mignosa 2024 115-116 no.2 figs.4-6 \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  ",{"id":187,"html":188},"handnote"," \u003Cp> Line 1  4-10  Interlineation line 1 to 2  not measured  \u003C/p>",{"id":190,"html":191},"license"," Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence ",[193,195,198,199],{"html":194},"Text encoding: 